ROX-Filer 2.12 GTK3 - r20 - 2026-07-26

GTK3 hidden-files toolbar icon
--------------------------------

- Changed the Hidden toolbar action to prefer the `cab_view` eye icon from the
  active GTK3 icon theme.

- Added a cross-theme fallback chain: `cab_view`, `view-hidden-files`,
  `view-hidden-files-symbolic`, `view-reveal` and `view-reveal-symbolic`.

- The bundled `rox-show-hidden` image is now used only as a final compatibility
  fallback when the active icon theme contains none of the supported names.

- The toolbar icon now follows Puppy/GTK3 icon-theme changes without depending
  on a theme-specific copy of the historical ROX image.

ROX-Filer 2.12 GTK3 - r19 - 2026-07-26

Standard Trash and batch deletion
---------------------------------

- The normal Delete key now moves selected items to the standard Freedesktop
  Trash through GIO, matching the behaviour of PCManFM, EssoraFM and other
  GTK file managers.
- Added a compact ROX-style confirmation with small action buttons.
- Added a separate Delete Permanently action on Shift+Delete.
- Permanent deletion asks once for the whole selection instead of once per
  file, then refreshes only the selected top-level paths.
- Moving a directory to Trash no longer recursively processes every file; the
  complete directory is moved by the GIO trash backend.
- Filesystems without Trash support report a clear error and are never silently
  converted to permanent deletion.
- Choice dialogs are exempt from the 640x400 work-window minimum so they retain
  the compact traditional ROX appearance.
- Added translations and precompiled message catalogues for all languages
  maintained by this GTK3 port.

ROX-Filer 2.12 GTK3 r18 - 2026-07-26

Compact ROX-style conflict buttons
----------------------------------

- Replaced the oversized 2x2 conflict-policy grid with compact action buttons
  in the standard GtkDialog action area.
- The dialog now follows the visual layout of the original ROX-Filer copy
  window, with small buttons aligned along the bottom.
- Removed the forced 640 x 400 size from this selector and exempted it from the
  global minimum used by normal filer windows.
- The available policies remain Ask, Skip all, Newer and Replace all.
- Added tooltips containing the complete policy descriptions.
- Ask remains the safe default and can be activated with Enter.
- Added the compact Ask translation to the Arabic and Catalan catalogues and
  rebuilt their bundled .mo files.

ROX-Filer 2.12 GTK3 r17 - 2026-07-26

ROX-style conflict policy buttons
---------------------------------

- Replaced the conflict-policy drop-down menu with four large, visible buttons.
- The available actions remain: ask for each conflict, replace existing files,
  skip existing files, and replace only when the source is newer.
- Arranged the choices in a compact two-by-two grid inside the 640 x 400 dialog.
- Added standard themed icons to each choice for faster visual recognition.
- The Ask button is the safe default and can be activated with Enter.
- The Cancel button remains separate in the normal GTK/ROX dialog action area.
- Reused the existing translated strings, so the button interface is available
  in every language already included with the rsync conflict dialog.
- Kept the per-file "Apply this decision to all remaining conflicts" option
  when the user chooses to ask for each conflict.

ROX-Filer 2.12 GTK3 r16 - 2026-07-26

Fast rsync copy and move engine
-------------------------------

- Added a hybrid file-operation engine based on rsync for faster local copies.
- Copying a directory now uses one rsync process for the complete directory
  tree instead of launching a separate cp process for every regular file.
- Multiple selected files and directories are copied in one rsync batch when
  their destination types are compatible.
- Moves inside the same filesystem continue to use the fast rename/mv path.
- Moves across filesystems and directory merges use rsync with
  --remove-source-files, followed by safe removal of directories that are
  actually empty.
- Added --partial so an interrupted rsync copy can retain partial transfer data.
- Added an automatic fallback to the classic ROX-Filer engine when rsync is not
  installed.
- The fallback remains fully functional and now also honours the selected
  conflict policy.

Conflict handling
-----------------

- Added a single conflict-policy dialog when destination items already exist.
- Available choices are: ask for each conflict, replace existing files, skip
  existing files, or replace only when the source is newer.
- Added "Apply this decision to all remaining conflicts" to the classic
  per-conflict comparison dialog.
- Replacing or skipping all remaining conflicts no longer requires pressing
  Enter or clicking a button for every individual file.
- Conflict decisions apply only to the current operation and are reset before
  the next copy or move.
- Added translated rsync errors, completion messages and conflict controls.

Internationalisation
--------------------

- Added all new rsync and conflict-policy strings to Arabic, Catalan, German,
  Spanish, French, Italian, Portuguese, Japanese, Hungarian, Russian,
  Simplified Chinese and Traditional Chinese catalogues.
- Rebuilt the bundled .mo catalogues, including generic pt and zh aliases.
- Catalogues remain inside the ROX AppDir under ROX-Filer/Messages; no duplicate
  installation under /usr/share/locale is required.

ROX-Filer 2.12 GTK3 r15 - 2026-07-26

GTK3 folder icon theme correction
---------------------------------

- Fixed normal directory icons using an old `inode_directory.png` MIME override
  instead of the standard folder icon from the active GTK3 icon theme.
- Normal folders now request `folder` first and use `folder-symbolic` only as a
  fallback.
- Legacy MIME-icons remain available for other MIME types but can no longer
  override the colour and appearance of ordinary folders.
- Removed the historical `inode-directory.png` and `inode-mount-point.png`
  links to `/usr/lib/X11/pixmaps/folder48.png`, which forced Puppy's old folder
  colour instead of the active GTK3 icon theme.
- Per-directory `.DirIcon` images and AppDir icons continue to take priority.
- Added automatic icon-cache invalidation when the active GTK3 icon theme
  changes, allowing folder icons to refresh without restarting ROX-Filer.

ROX-Filer 2.12 GTK3 r14
--------------------------
- Partitions is now the permanent first toolbar item, before Up.
- Partition filtering now follows EssoraWM's exact lsblk conditions.
- Successful lsblk results are no longer mixed with broad sysfs/runtime scans.
- ROX-Filer respects ~/.config/essorawm/hidden-drives.
- Puppy/sysfs detection remains only as a fallback when lsblk is unavailable.

ROX-Filer 2.12 GTK3 r13
------------------------

- Fixed the GTK3 icon-view scrollbar for directories containing more items
  than fit in the visible window. GtkViewport now uses the collection's
  natural vertical size instead of its small minimum requisition, allowing
  access to every visible file in large directories such as /usr/bin.
- The fix preserves the normal hidden-file option: dot files remain hidden
  until the user enables hidden files.

ROX-Filer 2.12 GTK3 r12 - 2026-07-26
-------------------------------------------
- Replaced the fragile incremental collection update search with linear pointer
  matching before sorting. Metadata changes from TYPE_UNKNOWN to a real file
  type can no longer make items disappear from the icon view.
- Added an authoritative end-of-scan verification against Directory.known_items.
  If even one visible item is missing, duplicated or stale, the view is rebuilt
  from the complete directory contents.
- Forced a full GTK3 layout recalculation after scanning so the viewport and
  scrollbar include every visible row.
- Locked the safe display order to folders first and all remaining visible files
  afterwards, sorted by name. Removed the Sort button from the toolbar.
- Expanded partition detection to combine lsblk, Puppy runtime drive_* entries
  and /sys/class/block partitions, while preventing duplicate devices.
- Relaxed the partition acceptance rule to match EssoraWM and include real
  partitions even when old Puppy lsblk versions omit TYPE or filesystem data.
- Kept hidden files controlled exclusively by the existing Hidden button.
- Added or updated josejp2424 attribution comments in every modified block.

ROX-Filer 2.12 GTK3 r11 - 2026-07-26
-------------------------------------------
- Enforced a real 640x400 minimum directly on every normal filer window,
  including windows restored from an older saved geometry and automatic
  icon-layout resizes.
- Disabled inherited, per-directory and glob filters in the normal filer view
  so every visible folder and every visible file is always displayed.
- Kept hidden-file visibility controlled only by the existing Hidden button.
- Moved the permanent Partitions button immediately after Up and added a
  fallback insertion path so it cannot disappear because of old toolbar
  customisation settings.
- Replaced the one-dimensional partition menu with a GTK3 popover containing a
  four-column grid. Additional units continue on the next row in groups of four.
- Kept drive-harddisk as the standard icon-theme name for the permanent button.
- Added or updated josejp2424 attribution comments in every modified block.

ROX-Filer 2.12 GTK3 r10 - 2026-07-26
-------------------------------------------
- Fixed the partition toolbar build failure caused by drives.h including
  global.h a second time while compiling drives.c.
- Replaced that include with a forward declaration of FilerWindow, preventing
  duplicate enum and typedef declarations such as MINI_NONE and TYPE_FILE.
- Kept drive-harddisk as the standard system icon for the permanent partition
  button, with the existing symbolic theme fallback.

ROX-Filer 2.12 GTK3 r9 - 2026-07-26
------------------------------------------
- Added a permanent Partitions button to the filer toolbar. It cannot be
  disabled through toolbar customisation.
- Reused the EssoraWM drive-detection approach to list real internal and
  removable partitions while filtering loop, Puppy runtime, swap and EFI
  technical volumes. Added a compatible lsblk fallback for older Puppy builds.
- Added mount-and-open behaviour: Puppy/root uses /bin/mount under /mnt and
  regular users can fall back to udisksctl. Mounted partitions open in the
  current ROX-Filer window.
- Set 640x400 as the minimum size for every normal ROX-Filer window and dialog,
  excluding panels, pinboards, menus, tooltips and desktop surfaces.
- Changed new filer windows and Preferences to 640x400.
- Removed the Dirs/Files-only toolbar filter that could accidentally hide
  tar.gz, AppImage, scripts and other normal files.
- Made directories remain first for every sort criterion, including descending
  order and both icon and detailed views.
- Added complete translations for the new partition interface strings in
  Arabic, Catalan, German, Spanish, French, Italian, Portuguese, Japanese,
  Hungarian, Russian, Simplified Chinese and Traditional Chinese.
- Marked every new or modified block with josejp2424 attribution comments.
- Added the GPLv3 text as LICENSE and documented this modified GTK3 release as
  GPL-3.0-or-later while retaining all original upstream notices.

